<!--
  Grid cell background. It is set on the thumbnail itself — the snapshot is the whole card in this
  style — and so also supplies the outline the ImageView clips its bitmap to, which is what rounds
  the corners of the snapshot.

  16dp, not the 20dp the List and Stack cards use: a Grid cell is a third of the screen wide, and
  measuring the reference (One UI 8, 1080x2400 @ 420dpi) puts the corner arc at 40px ≈ 15.2dp on a
  313px-wide card. Carrying the family's 20dp over would visibly over-round a card this small.

  The fill is the near-black an empty snapshot well should be, so a card whose bitmap has not
  arrived yet reads as a dim placeholder rather than flashing a bright block.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#FF17181C" />
    <corners android:radius="16dp" />
</shape>
